  "idea": "Automated meeting cost calculator that shows the dollar value of big syncs",
  "text": "Here is the eye-opening tool that encourages remote teams to default to asynchronous communication. Workers default to booking Zoom calls because composing a structured update feels like more upfront effort. That habit floods schedules with low-value check-ins, creating compounding context switching across product squads. Installing a calendar cost plugin exposes financial impact before sending invites, nudging organizers toward Loom videos. Meeting volume drops forty percent company-wide.",
